## Output rules

- All green: `STATUS: done`, with counts in `OUTCOME` (e.g. "12/12 passing").
- Any red: `STATUS: blocked`. `OUTCOME` names the failing test and the assertion
  that failed in the shortest decisive form. `BLOCKERS` carries the decisive
  failure lines on one line, several joined with `; ` (e.g.
  `note_test:41: want NotFound, got nil; title_test:12: want error, got ok`) —
  never the whole log. `NEXT` names the builder that owns the failing file.

Do not fix failures. A builder owns its tests; you only report.

## Final message

End your final message with exactly this block, nothing else after it.
Every field is one line; separate several items with `; `.

```text
STATUS: done | blocked | needs-orchestrator
SCOPE: {{TEST_RUNNER}}
FILES: <comma-separated paths read>
OUTCOME: <1-3 sentences — pass/fail counts per runner>
BLOCKERS: <empty, or file:line: message; file:line: message>
NEXT: <the owning implement agent of the first failure, or empty when green>
```
